# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# --- frontend --------------------------------------------------------------

node_modules/

# Vite output. `.gitkeep` keeps the directory around because main.go embeds
# `all:frontend/dist`; without it a fresh clone would fail to compile.
frontend/dist/*
!frontend/dist/.gitkeep

# Wails generated bindings. The frontend talks to the backend through the
# hand written bridge in src/api, so these are build artefacts only.
frontend/wailsjs/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/package.json.md5

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------------

build/bin/
dist/
*.log

# Generated by `wails build` from build/appicon.png (`just icons` deletes it so
# that a new logo actually propagates). Committing it would pin a stale icon.
build/windows/icon.ico

# Local-only reference screenshots used while matching the Navicat layout. They
# are somebody else's UI, so they stay out of the repository history.
/1.png
/2.png

# Scratch file for a long commit message (`git commit -F`), written by hand
# during a round of work. It is not part of the project.
.git-commit-msg.txt
